Compile this device code with nvcc for Volta or newer, for example `nvcc -arch=sm_70 -c broadcast.cu`. The usage contract is that all 32 non-exited lanes of a full physical warp call this function at the corresponding invocation, each supplying its float. The ballot produces `0x0007ffff`; exactly lanes 0–18 execute the shuffle with that identical mask, and lane 18 is a participating source, so every one of those nineteen callers receives its float. Lanes 19–31 execute the ballot but never the shuffle, and return their original values; no implicit lockstep, shared memory, atomics, or additional barrier is needed.
